! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1260 TEST 7's LAST BLOCK -- the between-
! bounds check under boundary control 1, the two UB+1 checks under
! boundary control 0, the SWEEP TEARDOWN, and the I60122 exit.
! PDF p.74, octal 022461.00-022512.40, 50 rows / 52 half-words,
! transcribed VERBATIM at the listing's own addresses and checked
! bit-exactly by verify_ax5b_160_test7_sweep_listing.py.  (This deck's
! listing pages carry NO printed page numbers; cite PDF pages only.)
!
! WHERE IT SITS.  Three files now cover TEST 7 end to end and none of
! them overlaps:
!
!   ax5b_160105_compare.strap        p.71   022346.40-022401.00  driver
!   ax5b_160_test7_compare.strap     pp.72-73 022401.40-022460.40 verdict
!   ax5b_160_test7_sweep.strap       p.74   022461.00-022512.40  THIS
!
! The premise was checked before a line was written: grepping every
! strap/verify_*.py for 022461 through 022512 found the range's
! addresses only in verify_ax5b_160_test7_compare_listing.py's PROSE
! (its "THE CUT POINT" paragraph and its 0-31 carve-out analysis) and
! in its SYN/bit-18 lines, never in a ROWS entry.  The range was
! genuinely untranscribed.
!
! WHAT IT ADDS TO THE ORACLE.  pp.72-73 witnessed BC 1 with an inside
! address (no signal) and BC 0 with an inside address (signal).  This
! page adds the two cases that complete the truth table:
!
!   I60121 (022461.00-022470.00)  BC 1, comparand INSIDE  -> NO signal
!       022463.00  TI,1,BOUND1,3.0    the control bit is ONE
!       022465.00  LX,$X13,0($X2)   -FETCH FRM LB+1, UB-1, BC IS 1.
!       022466.40  BZDFZ,I60212     branch on DF OFF -- the OK path
!       022467.00  SIC,SEN          -FETCH BETWEEN UB AND LB,
!       022467.40  B,SERS           -BC 1, CAUSES DF TO SET.
!
!   I60212 (022472.40-022502.00)  BC 0, comparand OUTSIDE -> NO signal
!       022474.40  TI,1,BOUND0,3.0    the control bit flips to ZERO
!       022475.40  V+I,$X2,2.0        X2 := LB+3 = UB+1
!       022477.00  LX,$X13,0($X2)     the UB+1 fetch (no comment row)
!       022500.40  BZDFZ,I60214     branch on DF OFF -- the OK path
!       022501.00  SIC,SEN          -FETCH FROM UB+1, BC 0, CAUSES
!       022501.40  B,SERS           -DF TO BE SET.
!
! With p.71's "UB signals under BC 1" and p.73's "LB+1 signals under
! BC 0", all four cells of (inside/outside) x (BC 0/BC 1) are now
! witnessed by rows this project has transcribed.  Reference Manual
! C22-6530-2 printed p.31: "When the boundary control bit is zero, a
! signal is obtained for a comparand inside the specified area.  When
! the boundary control bit is one, a signal is obtained for a
! comparand outside the specified area."
!
! THE SWEEP TEARDOWN, and it is the reason the loop ever stops:
!
!       022504.40  I60214 LV,$X2,$X2   -DONE ALL COMPS.
!       022505.00  BXVZ,I60122         -YES
!       022505.40  V-I,$X2,2.0         -NO
!       022506.00  BD,I60106
!
! LV,$X2,$X2 loads X2's value field from X2's OWN storage word (index
! registers X1-X15 are storage locations 17-31; $X2 = word 0o22, and
! the printed code "22.04 30" has exactly 0o22 in its address field).
! It changes nothing.  Its whole purpose is to SET THE INDEX RESULT
! INDICATORS, because the rows between the last V+I and here loaded
! and stored X13, not X2.  Reference Manual printed p.23: "Load Value
! (LV).  The value field, bits 0-24, of the index word specified by J
! is replaced by bits 0-24 of the half-word specified by bits 0-18 of
! the effective address", and "The index result indicators are set in
! all cases in which the index flag indicator is set, except the index
! comparison operations."  Then BXVZ tests it -- printed p.23 again:
! "Index Value Zero (XVZ).  This indicator is set to one when the
! value field is zero."
!
! BRANCH POLARITY, determined from THIS page's own rows and not
! assumed: B<IND> branches when the indicator is ON, BZ<IND> when it
! is OFF, a trailing Z clears it.  The two check triples here are
! 022466.40/022467.00/022467.40 and 022500.40/022501.00/022501.40, and
! in both the BRANCH is the OK path while the FALL-THROUGH is the
! SIC,SEN / B,SERS error pair.  So the error text names the ANOMALY:
! "-BC 1, CAUSES DF TO SET." is printed on the path taken when DF WAS
! set and should not have been.  (Routine 1274 elsewhere in this deck
! has the opposite shape, SIC,SEN first and a branch TO SERS.  This
! block is not that shape.)
!
! THE ERROR MESSAGES AND HEADINGS, verbatim with their octal
! locations, read at 600 dpi:
!
!   022464.00  -RESTORE MY INT.
!   022465.00  -FETCH FRM LB+1, UB-1, BC IS 1.
!   022466.00  -RESTORE INT.
!   022467.00  -FETCH BETWEEN UB AND LB,
!   022467.40  -BC 1, CAUSES DF TO SET.
!   022470.40  -RESTORE INT.
!   022471.00  -FETCH BETWEEN UB AND LB, BC 1,
!   022471.40  -CAUSES AD INTERRUPT, TESTING DONE.
!   022476.00  -RESTORE MY INT.
!   022500.00  -RESTORE INT.
!   022501.00  -FETCH FROM UB+1, BC 0, CAUSES
!   022501.40  -DF TO BE SET.
!   022502.40  -RESTORE INT.
!   022503.00  -FETCH FROM UB+1, BC 0, CAUSES AD
!   022503.40  -INTERRUPT, TESTING DONE
!   022504.40  -DONE ALL COMPS.
!   022505.00  -YES
!   022505.40  -NO
!   022506.40  -CLR BOUNDS REG.
!   022510.40  -TO SSIP.
!   022511.40  -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
!
! THREE DECK QUIRKS IN THAT LIST, all measured, none scan damage:
!   * "FRM" for FROM at 022465.00, the same garble pp.72-73 records at
!     022444.40 on the mirror-image row.
!   * "-BC 1, CAUSES DF TO SET." at 022467.40 against "-DF TO BE SET."
!     at 022501.40: the deck says "TO SET" in one message and "TO BE
!     SET" in its twin.
!   * "-INTERRUPT, TESTING DONE" at 022503.40 has NO terminating
!     period, where its twin "-CAUSES AD INTERRUPT, TESTING DONE." at
!     022471.40 has one.  Checked at 8x on the 600 dpi render: the
!     character cell after the E is empty.
!
! EVERY PRINTED LOCATION IN RANGE CARRIES MACHINE CODE.  There is no
! row here with a location and a blank code column, so no SLC gap and
! no SYN stand-in is needed anywhere inside 022461.00-022512.40.
!
! ENCODING ONLY, same reason as the other two files: the block cannot
! run without SSIP's save/restore at 001301/001304/001310/001311 and
! BOUND0/BOUND1 at 023302/023303.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS, and the SYN-naming rule stated so the split does not
! read as accidental.  This paragraph used to open "numeric labels are
! prefixed 'L' exactly as ax5b_160105_compare.strap and
! ax5b_160_test7_compare.strap do (L160121, L16012A, L160211, L160212,
! L16021B, L160213, L160214, L160122, plus the externals L160105,
! L160106, L160107, L16010A)", and to close by calling the leading
! glyph of IC260 letter-I by HOUSE CONVENTION and not by measurement.
! Both halves have been overtaken by the same measurement: at 600 dpi
! this chain's digit 1 carries an upper-left flag and a base serif at
! 30-42 px while the bare stroke runs 9-18, and no name field in
! either deck leads with the flagged glyph.  The labels are therefore
! I60121, I6012A, I60211, I60212, I6021B, I60213, I60214, I60122,
! I60105, I60106, I60107, I6010A and IC260 -- one reading, measured
! rather than conventional, and all of them legal STRAP-1 symbols
! without a prefix (docs/listing_typography.md).  The pp.72-73 file
! records the same correction.  "0%$X2(0)" is written "0($X2)", as in
! both adjacent files.  SEN,
! SERS, SEN0 and SSW keep the adjacent file's spelling.  ONE "L"
! SURVIVES and it is not a legality workaround: LBIT10 keeps the form
! ax5b_160_test8b.strap gives the bit table (LBIT11 / LBIT57), so the
! same constant has one name across routine 1260.
!
! I60121 AND I60122 ARE *DEFINED* HERE, not SYN'd.  pp.72-73 had to
! assume both (I60121 SYN,(8)22461.0 and I60122 SYN,(8)22506.40);
! this file's rows 1 and 42 put real labels at those two addresses, so
! the adjacent file's two assumptions are now witnessed.

I60105 SYN, (8)22346.40
I60106 SYN, (8)22356.0
I60107 SYN, (8)22372.0
I6010A SYN, (8)22371.40
BOUND0  SYN, (8)23302.0
BOUND1  SYN, (8)23303.0
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0
SEN0    SYN, (8)1311.0
SSW     SYN, (8)1301.0
IC260  SYN, (8)22737.0
LBIT10  SYN, (8)24534.0
        SLC, (8)22461.0
I60121 LVI, $X13, I60211
        SVA, $X13, I60107
        LVI, $X3, I6012A
        SVA, $X3, I6010A
        TI,  1, BOUND1, 3.0
        SR,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE MY INT.
        BE,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, 0($X2)        ! -FETCH FRM LB+1, UB-1, BC IS 1.
        BD,  $+.32
I6012A SV,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE INT.
        BZDFZ, I60212
        SIC, SEN                 ! -FETCH BETWEEN UB AND LB,
        B,   SERS                ! -BC 1, CAUSES DF TO SET.
        B,   I60212
I60211 SV,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE INT.
        SIC, SEN                 ! -FETCH BETWEEN UB AND LB, BC 1,
        B,   SERS                ! -CAUSES AD INTERRUPT, TESTING DONE.
        B,   I60122
I60212 LVI, $X13, I60213
        SVA, $X13, I60107
        LVI, $X3, I6021B
        SVA, $X3, I6010A
        TI,  1, BOUND0, 3.0
        V+I, $X2, 2.0
        SR,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE MY INT.
        BE,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, 0($X2)
        BD,  $+.32
I6021B SV,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE INT.
        BZDFZ, I60214
        SIC, SEN                 ! -FETCH FROM UB+1, BC 0, CAUSES
        B,   SERS                ! -DF TO BE SET.
        BD,  I60214
I60213 SV,  $X1, $IA            ! -RESTORE INT.
        SIC, SEN                 ! -FETCH FROM UB+1, BC 0, CAUSES AD
        B,   SERS                ! -INTERRUPT, TESTING DONE
        B,   I60122
I60214 LV,  $X2, $X2            ! -DONE ALL COMPS.
        BXVZ, I60122            ! -YES
        V-I, $X2, 2.0            ! -NO
        BD,  I60106
I60122 Z,   3.0                 ! -CLR BOUNDS REG.
        B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I60105
        SIC, SEN0+.32
        B,   SSW                 ! -TO SSIP.
        BD,  $+.32
        LX,  $X13, IC260        ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+,  $X13, LBIT10
        SX,  $X13, IC260
        END, I60121
